  id: Fornix_Dexter(Right_Side)
  partName: Fornix Dexter (Right Side)
  descriptionChunks:
  - The right fornix is a C-shaped bundle of nerve fibers within the limbic system
    that serves as a major communication pathway between the hippocampus and other
    brain regions. It plays a critical role in memory processing, learning, and emotional
    regulation.
  - This structure transmits signals that support coordination between cognitive
    and behavioral functions. By linking key neural centers, it ensures efficient
    information flow, contributing to memory formation and recall. Its proper function
    is essential for maintaining stable emotional responses and supporting higher-level
    brain activities.
